5. 32-BIT REGISTER ENCODING TABLE
-----------------------------------
How the REG and R/M bit patterns map onto the eight 32-bit
general-purpose registers:

  REG  | Register
  000  | EAX
  001  | ECX
  010  | EDX
  011  | EBX
  100  | ESP
  101  | EBP
  110  | ESI
  111  | EDI

-- 32-bit addressing forms with the ModR/M byte --

Mod = 00, Memory, no displacement:

  Eff. Addr \ R/M | 000 | 001 | 010 | 011 | 100 | 101 | 110 | 111
  [EAX]       000 | 00  | 08  | 10  | 18  | 20  | 28  | 30  | 38
  [ECX]       001 | 01  | 09  | 11  | 19  | 21  | 29  | 31  | 39
  [EDX]       010 | 02  | 0A  | 12  | 1A  | 22  | 2A  | 32  | 3A
